This is a MODIFIED version of xwax, forked for Waxcode DVS.
============================================================

Modified by Matt Hall, 2026. Upstream xwax is by Mark Hills and lives at
http://xwax.org/ - this fork is not affiliated with or endorsed by it.

Waxcode DVS runs xwax headless on a Raspberry Pi, driven over a control
socket by a Node server and an iOS app. See https://www.waxcode.co/

Changes from upstream include:

  - a control socket for headless operation (control.c, PROTOCOL.md)
  - key lock / master tempo via Rubber Band (keylock.c)
  - inverse RIAA equalisation for phono-level output (riaa.c)
  - cue point offsets, loop handling and playhead corrections
  - an acquire/release barrier on track length, for ARM64

Released under the GNU General Public License, version 3 - the same terms
as upstream. See the COPYING file.


xwax: Digital vinyl on Linux

(C) Copyright 2026 Mark Hills <mark@xwax.org>

For installation instructions, see the INSTALL file. Instructions can
be found in the xwax(1) man page and http://xwax.org/

"xwax" is a digital vinyl system (DVS) for Linux. It allows DJs and
turntablists to playback digital audio files (MP3, Ogg Vorbis, FLAC,
AAC and more), controlled using a normal pair of turntables via
timecoded vinyls.

